id: pm-rl-mxe0
title: "changelog:full and changelog:check use different projections"
description: "The regeneration command uses mode replace with all release tags, while the mandatory check uses mode prepend from the previous tag. After closing any new PM item, npm run changelog:full succeeds but npm run changelog:check immediately rejects the generated file and proposes an incompatible projection. Align the check with the package-owned full regeneration contract."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-06T22:57:42.945Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-06T22:58:02.219Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-06T22:58:01.789Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-06T22:58:01.789Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "changelog:full and changelog:check use identical mode, release-tag, version, date, URL, and release-respect inputs except for --check; regeneration followed by check passes; the full release gate passes"
severity: high
environment: pm-changelog 2026.8.6
repro_steps: "Run npm run changelog:full followed by npm run changelog:check on the current tracker."
resolution: "Made changelog:check use the same replace and all-release-tags projection as changelog:full, retaining the version, fixed date, item URL, and release filtering inputs."
expected_result: A freshly generated package changelog passes its mandatory check byte-for-byte.
actual_result: "The check adds entries that changelog:full omitted and fails the release gate."
affected_version: 2026.7.31
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T22:58:01.379Z",codex,"Before fix, changelog:full exited 0 and the immediately following changelog:check exited 1 with an incompatible prepend diff. The commands now differ only by --check."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  package.json,project,canonical changelog command contract
  CHANGELOG.md,project,regenerated canonical projection
tests[2]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,pm_context_mode}:
  "npm run changelog:full && npm run changelog:check",project,180,tracker
  "npm run release:check",project,900,tracker
close_reason: Aligned the generation and verification projections so a canonical regeneration is check-stable.
body: ""
